\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
If a pointed metric space M is uniformly discrete and its real Lipschitz-free Banach space has the approximation property, must that free space have the bounded approximation property for some finite constant?

\subsection{Short English statement}
If a pointed metric space M is uniformly discrete and its real Lipschitz-free Banach space has the approximation property, must that free space have the bounded approximation property for some finite constant?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Failure-of-Bounded-Approximation-in-a-Lipschitz-Free-Space-over-a-Uniformly-Discrete-Metric-Space-September-26-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

